---
source: crates/news/tests/cli.rs
expression: "stdout_of(&[\"work\", \"--help\"])"
---
Dispatch: the background worker for code-only pools (net, cpu, docling)

Usage: news work [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --limit <N>           Return at most N list items (default 20; `jobs claim`: how many to claim, default 1)
      --pools <POOLS>       Pools to run, comma-separated: net, cpu, docling [default: net,cpu,docling]
      --fields <A,B>        Keep only these keys of each item, comma-separated
      --worker <WORKER>     Worker name recorded on leases
      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue a truncated list from its next_cursor
      --once                One maintenance pass and one claim round, then exit
      --max-seconds <SECS>  Stop claiming after this many seconds, finish in-flight jobs, exit
  -h, --help                Print help
